From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrii <andrii_chepurnyi@epam.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2025 12:12:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xen_pvdev: Do not assume Dom0 when changing directory
 permissions

Instead of forcing the owner to domid 0, read the directory permissions
and add xen_domid with the given permission to it.

Note that for other than Dom0 domain (non toolstack domain) the
"driver_domain" property should be set in domain config file for the
toolstack to create required directories in advance.

(cherry picked from commit 92cbabbbefb34f34f5abd8486dd2de8f3ebe9a4e)

Signed-off-by: Oleksandr Tyshchenko <oleksandr_tyshchenko@epam.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrii <andrii_chepurnyi@epam.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream fork / BSP-layer delta; not submitted upstream]
Origin: https://github.com/xen-troops/qemu commit 92cbabbbefb34f34f5abd8486dd2de8f3ebe9a4e
---
 hw/xen/xen-operations.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/xen/xen-operations.c b/hw/xen/xen-operations.c
index e00983ec4..ce2d13e4d 100644
--- a/hw/xen/xen-operations.c
+++ b/hw/xen/xen-operations.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 
 #include "hw/xen/xen_native.h"
 #include "hw/xen/xen_backend_ops.h"
+#include "hw/xen/xen_pvdev.h"
 
 /*
  * If we have new enough libxenctrl then we do not want/need these compat
@@ -285,7 +286,8 @@ static bool libxenstore_create(struct qemu_xs_handle *h, xs_transaction_t t,
                                unsigned int owner, unsigned int domid,
                                unsigned int perms, const char *path)
 {
-    struct xs_permissions perms_list[] = {
+    unsigned int num;
+    struct xs_permissions *tmp, perms_list[] = {
         {
             .id    = owner,
             .perms = XS_PERM_NONE,
@@ -300,6 +302,14 @@ static bool libxenstore_create(struct qemu_xs_handle *h, xs_transaction_t t,
         return false;
     }
 
+    tmp = xs_get_permissions(h->xsh, 0, path, &num);
+    if (tmp == NULL) {
+        xen_pv_printf(NULL, 0, "xs_get_permissions %s: failed\n", path);
+        return false;
+    }
+    perms_list[0].id = tmp[0].id; /* retain the owner */
+    free(tmp);
+
     return xs_set_permissions(h->xsh, t, path, perms_list,
                               ARRAY_SIZE(perms_list));
 }
